String result = comp.compare(a, b) > 0 ? a : b;' After the quick-fix is applied: 'Comparator<String> comp = Comparator.naturalOrder();
String result = comp.max(a, b);' This inspection depends on the Java feature 'Comparator min/max methods', which is available since Java 26. Inspection ID: ComparatorMinMaxCanBeUsed New in 2026.1

