**Example:**


      public final class Main {
      }

After the quick-fix is applied:


      public class Main {
      }

Inspection ID: FinalClass

fullDescription.text:
Reports 'final' methods in 'final' classes. Since 'final' classes cannot be inherited, marking a method as 'final' may be unnecessary and confusing. Example: 'record Bar(int a, int b) {
  public final int sum() { 
     return a + b;
  }
}'
 After the quick-fix is applied: 'record Bar(int a, int b) {
  public int sum() { 
     return a + b;
  }
}' As shown in the example, a class can be marked as 'final' explicitly or implicitly. Inspection ID: FinalMethodInFinalClass

