Reports SLF4J, Log4j2 and akka.event.LoggingAdapter logging calls, such as 'logger.info("{}: {}", key)' where the number of '{}' placeholders in the logger message doesn't match the number of other arguments to the logging call. Use the inspection option to specify which implementation SLF4J uses. If Check automatically is chosen, then 'org.apache.logging.slf4j.Log4jLogger' is searched in the classpath. If this file is founded or Yes is chosen, then cases, when the last parameter with an exception type has a placeholder, will not be reported for SLFJ4 API. For example: '//this case will not be reported with "Yes" option
