Reports method parameters that are redundant and can be replaced with a local variable. If all usages of a parameter are preceded by an assignment to that parameter, the parameter can be replaced with a local variable. Such a parameter is unnecessary, as values that are passed to it are overwritten. Usually, the problem appears as a result of refactoring. Example: 'void test(int p) {
    p = 1;
    System.out.print(p);
  }' After the quick-fix is applied: 'void test() {
    int p = 1;
    System.out.print(p);
  }' Inspection ID: ParameterCanBeLocal

