Reports 'public' methods in classes which are not exposed in an interface. Exposing all 'public' methods via an interface is important for maintaining loose coupling, and may be necessary for certain component-based programming styles. Example: 'interface Person {
  String getName();
}

class PersonImpl implements Person {
  private String name;

  // ok: method is exposed in interface
  @Override
  public String getName() {
    return name;
