  }' Use the Warn everywhere declared exceptions may be thrown option to warn on method calls to methods that declare exceptions as well. Inspection ID: ThrowFromFinallyBlock

fullDescription.markdown:
Reports `throw` statements inside `finally` blocks. While occasionally intended, such `throw` statements can hide exceptions thrown from the `try` and `catch` blocks, thereby complicating the debugging process.

**Example:**


      class Fascinating {
        void doTask(Task t) {
          try {
            t.activity();
          } finally {
            if (!t.finish()) {
              throw new IllegalStateException();
            }
          }
        }
      }

Use the **Warn everywhere declared exceptions may be thrown** option
to warn on method calls to methods that declare exceptions as well.

Inspection ID: ThrowFromFinallyBlock

fullDescription.text:
Reports instantiations of 'Throwable' or its subclasses, where the created 'Throwable' is never actually thrown. Additionally, this inspection reports method calls that return instances of 'Throwable' or its subclasses, when the result of the method call is not thrown. Calls to methods annotated with the Error Prone's or AssertJ's '@CanIgnoreReturnValue' annotation will not be reported. Example: 'void check(String s) {
        if (s == null) {
            new NullPointerException("s");
        }
        // ...
    }' Inspection ID: ThrowableNotThrown

fullDescription.markdown:
Reports instantiations of `Throwable` or its subclasses, where the created `Throwable` is never actually thrown. Additionally, this inspection reports method calls that return instances of `Throwable` or its subclasses, when the result of the method call is not thrown.

Calls to methods annotated with the Error Prone's or AssertJ's `@CanIgnoreReturnValue` annotation will not be reported.

**Example:**


        void check(String s) {
            if (s == null) {
                new NullPointerException("s");
