Reports 'while' loops that could be more effectively written as 'do-while' loops. There are 'while' loops where the code just before the loop is identical to the code in the body of the loop. Replacing with a 'do-while' loop removes the duplicated code. For 'while' loops without such duplicated code, the quick fix is offered in the editor as well, but without highlighting. Example: 'foo();
