Reports string concatenation that can be converted to a string template. Using string templates is recommended as it makes code easier to read. Example: 'fun example() {
      val capitals = mapOf("France" to "Paris", "Spain" to "Madrid")
      for ((country, capital) in capitals) {
          print(capital + " is a capital of " + country)
      }
  }' After the quick-fix is applied: 'fun example() {
      val capitals = mapOf("France" to "Paris", "Spain" to "Madrid")
      for ((country, capital) in capitals) {
          print("$capital is a capital of $country")
      }
  }' Inspection ID: ConvertToStringTemplate

